Leo: Yes. I want to recommend The Old Man and the Sea by Hemingway.
Mia: Oh, I love that book. Why did you choose it?
Leo: It is short but powerful, and it teaches us never to give up.
Mia: That''s true. The old fisherman is so brave.
Leo: Exactly. What about you? What will you recommend?
Mia: I''ll recommend Pride and Prejudice. The characters feel so real.
Leo: Good choice. Let''s share both books with the club next week.', 'Mia 问 Leo 读书会要推荐哪本经典;Leo 想推荐海明威的《老人与海》,因为它短小却有力、教人永不放弃;Mia 说书中的老渔夫很勇敢;Mia 则要推荐《傲慢与偏见》,觉得人物很真实;两人决定下周把两本书都分享给读书会。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Which book does Leo want to recommend?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The Old Man and the Sea.","Pride and Prejudice.","War and Peace.","Journey to the West."]},{"q":"Why does Leo choose that book?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It is the longest book he owns.","It is short but powerful and teaches never to give up.","It is mainly about machines.","It has no real story."]},{"q":"What does Mia think of the old fisherman?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He is very brave.","He is rather lazy.","He is unkind to others.","He is very rich."]},{"q":"Which book will Mia recommend?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The Old Man and the Sea.","Pride and Prejudice.","A book of modern songs.","A book about history."]},{"q":"What will they do next week?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Close the book club for good.","Watch a film instead of reading.","Share both books with the club.","Return all the books unread."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U4', 'sufe');
He lived in the nineteenth century and wrote many famous books.
His stories often describe the hard lives of poor people in London.
Many of his novels, such as Oliver Twist, are still read today.
Through his writing, he hoped to make society kinder and fairer.', '查尔斯·狄更斯是最伟大的英国小说家之一;他生活在十九世纪,写了许多名著;他的故事常描写伦敦穷人的艰难生活;《雾都孤儿》等小说至今仍被阅读;他希望通过写作让社会更善良、更公正。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What was Charles Dickens?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A famous painter.","A king of England.","A modern scientist.","A great English novelist."]},{"q":"When did he live?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["In the nineteenth century.","In ancient times.","Only last year.","In the far future."]},{"q":"What do his stories often describe?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The lives of kings and queens.","The hard lives of poor people.","Life on distant planets.","How to build computers."]},{"q":"Which book is mentioned?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Hamlet.","Walden.","Oliver Twist.","The Old Man and the Sea."]},{"q":"What did Dickens hope to do through his writing?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Become a powerful king.","Stop people from reading.","Build many factories.","Make society kinder and fairer."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U4', 'sufe');
Lucy: Yes! I''m going to recite a poem by Wordsworth.
Tom: That sounds lovely. Which poem did you choose?
Lucy: Written in March. It''s full of the joy of spring.
Tom: I remember that one. Birds sing and the snow melts away.
Lucy: That''s right. What about you? Will you take part?
Tom: I''d like to, but I always get stage fright.
Lucy: Don''t worry. Just practise a lot, and you''ll feel braver.', 'Tom 问 Lucy 是否参加学校诗歌朗诵赛;Lucy 说要朗诵华兹华斯的诗;选的是《写于三月》,满是春天的喜悦;Tom 记得诗里鸟儿歌唱、积雪消融;Tom 想参加却总是怯场;Lucy 鼓励他多练习就会更勇敢。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What contest are they talking about?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A poetry recitation contest.","A singing contest.","A sports match.","A cooking show."]},{"q":"Which poem will Lucy recite?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A ci poem by Su Shi.","Written in March by Wordsworth.","A sonnet by Shakespeare.","A modern pop song."]},{"q":"What is the poem full of?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["The fear of winter.","The noise of cities.","The joy of spring.","The sadness of war."]},{"q":"Why is Tom unsure about taking part?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["He really hates poetry.","He has no free time.","He cannot read at all.","He often gets stage fright."]},{"q":"What does Lucy advise Tom to do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Practise a lot to feel braver.","Give up the idea at once.","Just stay at home.","Sing a song instead."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U4', 'sufe');
She wrote novels about love, family and daily life in the countryside.
Her most famous book is Pride and Prejudice.
Her characters feel clever, funny and very real.
Even today, millions of readers around the world enjoy her stories.', '简·奥斯丁是约两百年前的著名英国作家;她写关于爱情、家庭和乡村日常生活的小说;她最著名的书是《傲慢与偏见》;她笔下的人物聪明、风趣又十分真实;如今全世界仍有数百万读者喜爱她的故事。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"When did Jane Austen live?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only last week.","About two hundred years ago.","In ancient Rome.","In the distant future."]},{"q":"What did she write about?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["War and machines.","Space travel.","Love, family and country life.","Wild sea animals."]},{"q":"What is her most famous book?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Oliver Twist.","Walden.","The Old Man and the Sea.","Pride and Prejudice."]},{"q":"What are her characters like?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Clever, funny and very real.","Boring and flat.","Cruel and cold.","Strange and unreal."]},{"q":"Who still enjoys her stories today?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only her own family.","Millions of readers worldwide.","Nobody at all.","Only small children."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U4', 'sufe');
Ben: Great! I love that place. What are we going to do there?
Anna: A librarian will show us the room of old classic books.
Ben: Wonderful. Can we borrow some books too?
Anna: Yes, each of us can borrow up to three books.
Ben: Then I''ll borrow a novel and a book of poems.
Anna: Good idea. Remember to bring your library card.
Ben: I won''t forget. I''m really looking forward to it.', 'Anna 说本周五全班去市图书馆;Ben 很高兴,问去那里做什么;Anna 说馆员会带他们参观古旧经典藏书的房间;Ben 问能否借书;Anna 说每人最多可借三本;Ben 想借一本小说和一本诗集;Anna 提醒他带借书证;Ben 说不会忘,很期待。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where is the class going on Friday?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["To a sports field.","To the cinema.","To the city library.","To a factory."]},{"q":"What will the librarian show them?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A swimming pool.","A computer lab.","A flower garden.","A room of old classic books."]},{"q":"How many books can each student borrow?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Up to three.","Only one.","As many as ten.","None at all."]},{"q":"What will Ben borrow?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only some magazines.","A novel and a book of poems.","A film and a game.","Nothing at all."]},{"q":"What must Ben remember to bring?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["His football.","His lunch box.","His library card.","His umbrella."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U4', 'sufe');
Do not give up just because the first few pages seem difficult.
Read a little every day, and the story will slowly draw you in.
If you meet a hard word, try to guess its meaning from the sentence.
Step by step, you will discover why these classics have lasted so long.', '给想读经典的人一个小贴士:别因为开头几页难就放弃;每天读一点,故事会慢慢把你吸引进去;遇到生词,试着从句子里猜意思;一步步地,你就会发现这些经典为何流传至今。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who is this tip for?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only school teachers.","Only famous writers.","Only young children.","Anyone who wants to enjoy classic books."]},{"q":"What does the speaker advise about difficult first pages?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Don''t give up.","Stop reading for good.","Skip the whole book.","Throw the book away."]},{"q":"How often should you read?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only once a year.","A little every day.","Never at all.","Only during exams."]},{"q":"What should you do with a hard word?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Ignore the whole book.","Stop reading at once.","Guess its meaning from the sentence.","Copy it a hundred times."]},{"q":"What will you discover step by step?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["That reading is useless.","That classics are boring.","That books are too cheap.","Why these classics have lasted so long."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U4', 'sufe');

-- ===== 6) 写作 1篇 =====
DELETE FROM public.junior_writing_prompts WHERE publisher='sufe' AND volume='elective4' AND unit='U4';

"Are you kidding, Dad?" Ted hugged his father tightly. "It''s perfect. It''s the best birthday present I''ve ever had." He meant every word. As they rode together to the park that morning, Ted realised that the bike was not really old at all. It was full of his father''s love. He had wanted a shiny new racer, but what he received was far more precious, and he would treasure it for the rest of his life.', '【15 分制】A 档(13-15):五要素齐全、组织有条理、语言准确多样;B 档(10-12):要点较全、少量错误;C 档(7-9):要点偏少、句型简单;D 档(0-6):内容不完整、错误多。', '["For the first time he noticed how carefully the frame had been painted.","He thought of all the late nights his father must have spent in the cold garage.","Slowly, the disappointment in his heart began to melt away.","What he received was far more precious, and he would treasure it for the rest of his life."]'::jsonb, '[{"wrong":"Ted hugged to his father.","correct":"Ted hugged his father.","note":"hug 是及物动词,后面直接跟宾语,不加 to。"},{"wrong":"He wish he can keep the bike forever.","correct":"He wished he could keep the bike forever.","note":"wish 后从句用过去时(could)表示虚拟;主句 wished 也用过去式。"},{"wrong":"The bike made by his father.","correct":"The bike was made by his father.","note":"被动语态须有 be 动词:was made。"}]'::jsonb, '【读后续写结构(两段)】
第5段 下落动作:I know it''s not exactly what you wanted, but …（父亲的话 → Ted 注意到细节 → 想到父亲付出 → 失望消散）
第6段 结局:"Are you kidding, Dad?" Ted hugged his father.（拥抱 → 真心的话 → 一起骑车 → 升华:旧车满载父爱,学会感激）', 2, 'elective4', 'U4', 'sufe');

